  "title": "fix round 1: S1b cache_telemetry: per-invocation prompt-cache economics (hit ratio, effective cost, pre",
  "spec": "Fix round 1 for T-1058 (gate red: acceptance tests missing). The tests below were named in the acceptance but their files were outside the original write scope; this round adds tests/test_cli.py to the scope. Write exactly these tests as unittest.TestCase methods, matching the behaviour the merged implementation in this worktree already has (adjust the implementation only if a test exposes a real defect): tests/test_cli.py::test_scorecard_cache_is_exclusive_with_other_modes (scorecard --cache combined with another scorecard mode is rejected like the existing exclusive modes). Keep every other acceptance line green; run .claude/hooks/tests-green.sh . until it exits 0. Do not ask questions; report files changed and failures-only output.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_cache_telemetry.py::test_normalize_claude_and_codex_usage (both providers, hit_ratio bounds, zero-safe)",
    "tests/test_cache_telemetry.py::test_effective_cost_uses_pool_ratios (ratios from a temp pool.toml; defaults when the section is absent)",
    "tests/test_cache_telemetry.py::test_report_groups_by_role_provider_and_prefix_reuse (synthetic rows with repeated prefix_sha give reuse_rate)",
    "tests/test_spawn.py::test_packet_meta_carries_prefix_identity (prefix_sha stable when only task-specific sections change)",
    "tests/test_bus.py::test_log_run_annotates_cache_fields (row gets cache fields; annotate failure never raises)",
    "tests/test_cache_telemetry.py::test_annotate_reuses_existing_row_fields_and_adds_only_ratio_cost_prefix",
    "tests/test_cli.py::test_scorecard_cache_is_exclusive_with_other_modes",
    "tests/test_spawn.py::test_render_records_prefix_identity_before_packet_header (two tasks of one role with identical templates and tools share prefix_sha; suffix_chars differ)",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh exits 0",
    "fix round: the previously missing tests exist as unittest methods in tests/test_cli.py"
  ],
